            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for an arrow, then the Arabic for armour."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: في تلك الليلة",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "في تلك الليلة — fī tilka al-layla — \"that night\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "في تلك الليلة لم ينم أحد في البيت. fī tilka al-layla lam yanam aḥad fī al-bayt. That night nobody in the house slept."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "في تلك الليلة (fī tilka al-layla) is \"in that night\": layla, one night, is built on the inherited Semitic root l-y-l (Lane), the root of the taught layl; EtymDB sets it beside Hebrew laylā and Aramaic lēlyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
