          "title": "You'll want to know: إلى أن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "إلى أن — ilā an — \"until\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "انتظرنا إلى أن توقف المطر. intaẓarnā ilā an tawaqqafa al-maṭar. We waited until the rain stopped."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A verb follows: إلى أن (ilā an) وصل. Before a noun, say حتى."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "إلى أن (ilā an) joins the preposition ilā, \"to, as far as\", and an, \"that\": \"up to the time that\". Lane treats both as old particles; their origin beyond Arabic is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
